(6790139, 1018517, 109387, '<td valign="top">Very nice idea Margaret! Some advice to improve what, in any case, is a good result: Light on the tree (it comes from the right, so you could dodge and burn the tree to let the viewer understand the direction of light). Change the color balance of wings and use the clone stamp tool to improve the transition between the horse and the wings. You could add some horse shadows on the tree. But at first sight it looks beautiful, so these are more than baby steps in expert :)</td>', 'Very nice idea Margaret! Some advice to improve what, in any case, is a good result: Light on the tree (it comes from the right, so you could dodge and burn the tree to let the viewer understand the direction of light). Change the color balance of wings and use the clone stamp tool to improve the transition between the horse and the wings. You could add some horse shadows on the tree. But at first sight it looks beautiful, so these are more than baby steps in expert :)', '2012-06-08 05:17:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6790162, 1018493, 109387, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by grahamgator:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice detail.  Are those people on the ledges - my old eyes can''t tell. (voted earlier) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, little men watching their sun fading. We should be allowed to upload at least at 1000px, 800 sometimes is not enough :)</td>', 'Originally posted by grahamgator: Nice detail.  Are those people on the ledges - my old eyes can''t tell. (voted earlier)   Yes, little men watching their sun fading. We should be allowed to upload at least at 1000px, 800 sometimes is not enough :)', '2012-06-08 05:44:22.000000', NULL, 0),
