(6790319, 1018763, 138253, '<td valign="top">Regarding you comment on "doesn''t belong in expert editing", this is a misconception that many people have.<br/>You can still submit great shots like this without having to use all sorts of touch-up tools, it just gives you the opportunity to use them if you wish.</td>', 'Regarding you comment on "doesn''t belong in expert editing", this is a misconception that many people have.You can still submit great shots like this without having to use all sorts of touch-up tools, it just gives you the opportunity to use them if you wish.', '2012-06-08 09:17:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(6790323, 1018169, 138253, '<td valign="top">yeah, had a hard job focusing on this one. The action all seemed to go down so fast that i just took a few shots on continuous and this was the most clean of the group.<br/>I was doing the green macro while being buzzed by a fly, i was swatting at him to get away and a few seconds later noticed the spider on the move in the web.<br/> <br/>I tried to focus on the fly as much as i could because the spider is fairly obvious even blurred, and i thought if i could get a good shot with the fly in the web it would hold up even in an expert editing challenge.<br/> <br/>I''m *trying* to be ambitious in some of my recent shoots, they''re just not working out as well as i had hoped and i''ve had to scrap entire shoots because i just have flaws that most non-photographers would consider minor or inconsequential but would get me torn to shreds here.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the vote of confidence that I am getting better though, it''s great to hear and really means a lot! :)</td>', 'yeah, had a hard job focusing on this one. The action all seemed to go down so fast that i just took a few shots on continuous and this was the most clean of the group.I was doing the green macro while being buzzed by a fly, i was swatting at him to get away and a few seconds later noticed the spider on the move in the web. I tried to focus on the fly as much as i could because the spider is fairly obvious even blurred, and i thought if i could get a good shot with the fly in the web it would hold up even in an expert editing challenge. I''m *trying* to be ambitious in some of my recent shoots, they''re just not working out as well as i had hoped and i''ve had to scrap entire shoots because i just have flaws that most non-photographers would consider minor or inconsequential but would get me torn to shreds here. Thanks for the vote of confidence that I am getting better though, it''s great to hear and really means a lot! :)', '2012-06-08 09:25:07.000000', NULL, 0),
